window.docContents[220].resolve({"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Proof-by-Rewriting--General-Proofs-about-Natural-Numbers--Displaying-Theorem-Statements":{"contents":"The #check command can also be used to examine the statements of\npreviously declared lemmas and theorems.\n\n#check mul_zero\n#check mul_succ\n\n\nNatPlayground.Nat.mul_zero (n : Nat) : n * zero = zero\n\n\nNatPlayground.Nat.mul_succ (n m : Nat) : n * succ m = n * m + n\n\n\n\n\nLean displays universally quantified variables as binders before the colon, which is\nthe preferred declaration-header style in Lean.\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Basics: Functional Programming in Lean\u0009Proof by Rewriting\u0009General Proofs about Natural Numbers","header":"2.4.8.1. Displaying Theorem Statements","id":"/Basics/#Logical-Foundations--Basics___-Functional-Programming-in-Lean--Proof-by-Rewriting--General-Proofs-about-Natural-Numbers--Displaying-Theorem-Statements"}});